riate completed piece."},{"title":"Polish with Focused Rehearsal","objective":"Use a rehearsal plan to improve weak sections."},{"title":"Record and Reflect","objective":"Deliver and evaluate a complete performance."}],"practiceTitle":"Beginner Recital Rehearsal","practiceInstructions":"Run the piece in sections and as a complete performance using a recital checklist.","challengeTitle":"Beginner First Recital Challenge","evidence":"Recorded or approved live performance of one polished Beginner piece plus reflection.","rubric":[{"name":"Accuracy and continuity","weight":25},{"name":"Technique and posture","weight":20},{"name":"Rhythm and tempo","weight":20},{"name":"Expression and communication","weight":25},{"name":"Preparation and reflection","weight":10}],"aria":["recital planning","performance nerves","recovery","expression","constructive reflection"],"concern":"Repertoire, licensing, and recital accommodations require teacher approval."},{"level":2,"num":1,"title":"Chord Inversions","objective":"Use root position and first/second inversions to create smooth chord movement.","lessons":[{"title":"Triads and Inversion Labels","objective":"Construct and identify three triad positions."},{"title":"Voice Leading between Chords","objective":"Choose inversions that minimize motion."},{"title":"Inversions in a Pop Progression","objective":"Perform a progression with smooth voice leading."}],"practiceTitle":"Inversion Connection Drill","practiceInstructions":"Practice an approved progression using at least two inversions and minimal hand movement.","challengeTitle":"Smooth Chord Inversions Challenge","evidence":"Audio/video of a progression using root position and inversions with explanation.","rubric":[{"name":"Chord construction","weight":30},{"name":"Inversion accuracy","weight":25},{"name":"Voice leading","weight":20},{"name":"Rhythm and technique","weight":15},{"name":"Reflection and completeness","weight":10}],"aria":["inversion recognition","efficient fingering","v