 names."},{"title":"Intervals and Rhythm in Bass Clef","objective":"Read notes by interval while maintaining rhythm."},{"title":"Read a Short Bass Line","objective":"Perform a short unfamiliar bass line."}],"practiceTitle":"Bass-Clef Reading Cards","practiceInstructions":"Read short bass-clef patterns without writing every note name.","challengeTitle":"Bass-Clef Reading Challenge","evidence":"Video/live evidence of reading a teacher-selected bass line with brief strategy explanation.","rubric":[{"name":"Pitch reading","weight":30},{"name":"Rhythm reading","weight":25},{"name":"Continuity","weight":20},{"name":"Left-hand technique","weight":15},{"name":"Strategy and completeness","weight":10}],"aria":["landmarks","interval reading","left-hand mapping","rhythm","confidence"],"concern":"Source mnemonic appears as GDBDA and should be corrected/teacher-reviewed."},{"level":2,"num":8,"title":"Improvising with the Blues Scale","objective":"Create coherent improvised phrases with the blues scale over a stable accompaniment.","lessons":[{"title":"Build the Blues Scale","objective":"Construct and play an approved blues scale."},{"title":"Call and Response Phrasing","objective":"Use rests, repetition, and response."},{"title":"Develop a Short Solo","objective":"Shape a short solo across the blues form."}],"practiceTitle":"Blues Phrase Lab","practiceInstructions":"Create three short call-and-response phrases over a slow backing pattern.","challengeTitle":"Blues Scale Improvisation Challenge","evidence":"Audio/video of an improvised blues-scale solo with coherent phrases and reflection.","rubric":[{"name":"Scale-note control","weight":25},{"name":"Rhythm and phrasing","weight":25},{"name":"Form awareness","weight":20},{"name":"Expression and creativity","weight":20},{"name":"Reflection and completeness","weight":10}],"aria":["blue-note control","motif development","space","form","confidence"],"concern":"Backing track, key, and solo length require teacher approval."},{"level":2,"